<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">EOE: Evolutionary Optimization of Experts 
<br class="ltx_break">for Training Language Models</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Yingshi Chen
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_email"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Email: </span><a href="mailto:"><span id="id1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gsp.cys@gmail.com</span></a>
</span></span></span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">This paper presents an evolutionary framework for the training of large language models(LLM). The models are divided into several experts(sub-networks), which have the same structure but different parameter values. Only one expert is trained at each step. After the classical AdamW optimization, some evolutionary operators(crossover, PSO, and mutation) act on the tensor weights between the current expert and the best expert. So current expert would learn the experience of best expert. The direction of best expert would help current expert’s loss decrease faster. Finally, only save the weight of the best expert. Experiments show that best expert would achieve nearly the same accuracy as the full model. This would greatly reduce the size of the model for inference. Since only one expert is trained at each step, the training needs much less memory and has much higher throughput. Experiments show that the throughput would accelerate more than ten times! Our source code is available at <a href="https://github.com/gruai/koifish" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/gruai/koifish</a>. It’s a pure c++/cu framework, which is suitable for easy deployment on PCs and edge computing devices.</p>
  
</div>
<div id="id2" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_align_bottom">
    <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:2.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
    <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:2.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
    
<div id="p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">A Preprint
<br class="ltx_break"></span></p>
<table id="p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_top">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:0.0pt;height:24.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"></span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p id="p1.3" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">August 24, 2026</p>
</div>
  
</div>
<div id="p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">K</em><span id="p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">eywords</span> Evolutionary computation  <math id="p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math>
Large language models  <math id="p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math>
Sparse LLM  <math id="p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math>
Crossover Mutation  <math id="p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math>
Koifish</p>
</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Large language models(LLM)<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> opens the door to new era. But it’s too large and requires too many training resources. Even training a small model( 1B parameters) requires multiple GPUs. For example, it needs eight H100 GPUs and 24 hours to train a GPT-2 with 1558M parameters<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>. This poses a heavy burden on researchers and also hinders the rapid iteration and improvement of algorithms. A promising way to reduce train cost is using sparse structure, especially Mixture of Experts (MoE) architectures<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>. MoE is the cornerstone of Mixtral<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>, Gemini<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>, DeepSeek<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>, and more … Each MoE layer has a gating network and multiple sub-networks (“experts”). When a token is processed, the gating network routes it to one or a few experts, and their outputs are combined as the final output.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This paper presents a new sparse expert framework of evolutionary optimization of experts(EOE). As Figure <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ EOE: Evolutionary Optimization of Experts for Training Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> shows, it splits the full model into some equal-sized sub-networks(experts) and trains each sub-network one by one. These experts have the same structure, but their parameter values are different. They are fed with different tokens. They have different search paths and traversed different mountains and valleys in the solution space. Just like different particles of particle optimization algorithm(PSO)<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>, or different genes of genetic algorithm(GA)<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>, or different ants of ant colony optimization(ACO)<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>. So it’s natural to follow the evolutionary optimization process of these algorithms. Although the evolutionary operators(mutation, crossover, …) are different from the classical AdamW<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite> method, their essence is similar, that is, to find the model parameters (weights) <math id="S1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> that minimize the loss function <math id="S1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S1.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ EOE: Evolutionary Optimization of Experts for Training Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> lists some key difference between MoE and EOE framework.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S1.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Comparison of MoE models and EOE models</figcaption>
<table id="S1.T1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S1.T1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S1.T1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S1.T1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S1.T1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.T1.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S1.T1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S1.T1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Division method</span></th>
<th id="S1.T1.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S1.T1.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gating network</span></th>
<th id="S1.T1.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S1.T1.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S1.T1.2.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.T1.2.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inference model</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S1.T1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S1.T1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S1.T1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S1.T1.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">MoE(Mixture of Experts)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S1.T1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Split each FFN to some sub-networks</td>
<td id="S1.T1.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Yes</td>
<td id="S1.T1.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S1.T1.2.2.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S1.T1.2.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_p">Save all parameters</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S1.T1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S1.T1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S1.T1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S1.T1.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">EOE(Evolutionary Optimization of Experts)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S1.T1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Split all layers to some sub-networks</td>
<td id="S1.T1.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">No</td>
<td id="S1.T1.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S1.T1.2.3.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S1.T1.2.3.4.1.1" class="ltx_p">Only save parameters of best experts</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We have implemented EOE framework in an open source project <span id="S1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Koifish</span> at <a href="https://github.com/gruai/koifish" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/gruai/koifish</a> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>. Koifish is a pure c++/cu project, which needs much less training resources than other frameworks. The current version could train GPT-2 1558M model on a single 4090 GPU within 37 hours. While in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>, it takes eight H100 GPUs and 24 hours to train a GPT-2 1558M model.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S1.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.24436v1/EOE.png" id="S1.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/268;" width="381" height="268" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>An evolutionary optimization framework for the training of large language models(LLM)</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Method</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 2 Method ‣ EOE: Evolutionary Optimization of Experts for Training Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> describes the framework of evolutionary optimization of experts. There are mainly three steps:</p>
<ul id="S2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Divide model into multiple experts <math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}=\{\mathcal{E}_{1},\mathcal{E}_{2},...,\mathcal{E}_{N}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}=\{\mathcal{E}_{1},\mathcal{E}_{2},...,\mathcal{E}_{N}\}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Train the current expert using the classic AdamW optimization process,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The current expert learns the experience of the best expert <math id="S2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{best}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{best}</annotation></semantics></math> using the evolutionary optimization process.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Evolutionary training of LLM with multiple experts</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          Training dataset <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{\mathbf{x}_{1},\mathbf{x}_{2},...\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{\mathbf{x}_{1},\mathbf{x}_{2},...\}</annotation></semantics></math>. A batch <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> includes some shuffled token sequence <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          A model divided into multiple experts <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}=\{\mathcal{E}_{1},\mathcal{E}_{2},...,\mathcal{E}_{N}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}=\{\mathcal{E}_{1},\mathcal{E}_{2},...,\mathcal{E}_{N}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{best}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{best}</annotation></semantics></math> is the best expert with minimal loss.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
          Hyperparameter: learning rate <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, weight decay <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, crossover ratio <math id="alg1.l3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, mutation ratio <math id="alg1.l3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, …

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
          Trained model parameters <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each expert <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
            Load the parameters of <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
            Train this expert with some batches <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\mathcal{B}_{1},\mathcal{B}_{2},...,\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{B}_{1},\mathcal{B}_{2},...,\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each batch <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AdamW Optimization:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
             Compute loss <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Forward pass 
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{grads}\leftarrow\nabla_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">grads</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{grads}\leftarrow\nabla_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l11.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> backpropagation
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{(k+1)}\leftarrow\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{(k)}-\eta\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{m}}_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}/(\sqrt{\widehat{\mathbf{v}}_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}}+\epsilon)-\eta\lambda\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{(k+1)}\leftarrow\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{(k)}-\eta\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{m}}_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}/(\sqrt{\widehat{\mathbf{v}}_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}}+\epsilon)-\eta\lambda\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evolutionary Optimization:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{grads}\leftarrow\text{Mutation}(\texttt{grads},{r_{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">grads</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>Mutation</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">grads</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{grads}\leftarrow\text{Mutation}(\texttt{grads},{r_{m}})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{grads}\leftarrow\text{CrossOver}(\texttt{grads of $\mathcal{E}_{best}$},{r_{c}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">grads</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>CrossOver</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">grads of </mtext><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{grads}\leftarrow\text{CrossOver}(\texttt{grads of $\mathcal{E}_{best}$},{r_{c}})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Update best expert:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}&lt;\mathcal{L}_{best}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}&lt;\mathcal{L}_{best}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
            
            
               <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{best}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{best}</annotation></semantics></math> = <math id="alg1.l18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">21:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">22:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1 </span>Divide model into multiple experts</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A decoder-only transformer<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> model <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math> consists three component:</p>
<ol id="S2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Input component: A token embeddings layer( may followed by positional encoding as GPT-2). Its parameters are represented by <math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{in}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{in}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Stacked encoder component with <math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> blocks. Each block contains a multi-head self-attention(MHSA) layer and a position-wise Feed-Forward Network(FFN) layer. Koifish splits <math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> block into <math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> partitions. Its parameters <math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{encoder}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{encoder}</annotation></semantics></math> are split into <math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> partitions:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{encoder}=\{\theta_{1},\theta_{2},...,\theta_{K}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{encoder}=\{\theta_{1},\theta_{2},...,\theta_{K}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Output component:
A linear mapping layer(maps the last decoder’s output to unnormalized pre-logits) followed by a softmax layer to produce class probabilities. Its parameters are represented by <math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{out}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{out}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Koifish defines each expert <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> as a union of input component, output component, and one partition of encoder component. Its parameters are:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}=\{\theta_{in},\theta_{i},\theta_{out}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}=\{\theta_{in},\theta_{i},\theta_{out}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">These experts share the same input and output components. They are trained one by one. For each batch <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, only train and update the parameter of one expert. And the parameters of all other experts are fixed.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For distinction, we refer to the original model as <span id="S2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">full model</span> and <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}=\{\mathcal{E}_{1},\mathcal{E}_{2},...,\mathcal{E}_{N}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}=\{\mathcal{E}_{1},\mathcal{E}_{2},...,\mathcal{E}_{N}\}</annotation></semantics></math> as <span id="S2.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">EOE model</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>AdamW Optimization</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="S2.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Forward Pass:</span> Process a batch <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain the probability distribution of target tokens.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Loss Calculation:</span> Compute the average cross-entropy loss between the predicted logits and the true target tokens.</p>
<table id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}=-\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\log P(w_{t}|w_{&lt;t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mi>log</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=-\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\log P(w_{t}|w_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I3.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the batch size, and <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the true token at position <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S2.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Backward Propagation:</span> Calculate the gradients of the loss. Calculate the gradients of the parameters of current expert <math id="S2.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> via backpropagation.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S2.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameter Update:</span> Update current expert parameters <math id="S2.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> using the computed gradients. At the <math id="S2.I3.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th step, a typically used update rule of AdamW<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite> optimizer is:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{(k+1)}=\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{(k)}-\eta\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{m}}_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}/(\sqrt{\widehat{\mathbf{v}}_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}}+\epsilon)-\eta\lambda\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{(k)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{(k+1)}=\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{(k)}-\eta\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{m}}_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}/(\sqrt{\widehat{\mathbf{v}}_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}}+\epsilon)-\eta\lambda\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I3.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.I3.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I3.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{v}}</annotation></semantics></math> are bias-corrected estimates of the first and second moments of the gradients, respectively.
The parameters of all other experts are fixed.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.3 </span>Evolutionary Optimization</h3>

<div id="S2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The evolutionary optimization of EOE framework mainly used the following three evolutionary operators:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="S2.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S2.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Particle swarm</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.I4.i1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I4.i1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In many particle swarm algorithms(PSO)<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>: individuals always follow the direction of the leaders(best expert). Koifish uses a similar method to update the elements of current expert:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{j}=\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{j}+r_{social}*p*\cdot(\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{best}}^{j}-\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{j})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{j}=\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{j}+r_{social}*p*\cdot(\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{best}}^{j}-\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I4.i1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.I4.i1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{social}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{social}</annotation></semantics></math> is the social component of PSO and <math id="S2.I4.i1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is a random variable between <math id="S2.I4.i1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S2.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Crossover</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.I4.i2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I4.i2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The standard crossover operator of GA<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite> combines two tensors to produce new offsprings. Koifish adopt a one-way crossover: only current expert would copy some elements from the best expert with a low probability <math id="S2.I4.i2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{j}=\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{best}}^{j}\;\text{if}\;p&lt;r_{c}\;\text{otherwise}\;\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{j}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{j}=\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{best}}^{j}\;\text{if}\;p&lt;r_{c}\;\text{otherwise}\;\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I4.i2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.I4.i2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> is the ratio of crossover and <math id="S2.I4.i2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is a random variable.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S2.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mutation</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.I4.i3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I4.i3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Mutation operator is vital for maintaining diversity in genetic algorithm(GA)<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>. More diversity would reduce the possibility of getting stuck in the local minima. GA randomly modifies one or more genes of a chromosome with the mutation probability <math id="S2.I4.i3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>. Koifish use similar method. Each element of <math id="S2.I4.i3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> has a certain(very small) probability of gaussian mutation:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{j}=\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{j}+\mathcal{N}(0,s)\;\text{if}\;p&lt;r_{m}\;\text{otherwise}\;\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{j}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{j}=\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{j}+\mathcal{N}(0,s)\;\text{if}\;p&lt;r_{m}\;\text{otherwise}\;\theta_{\mathcal{E}_{i}}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I4.i3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<ul id="S2.I4.i3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S2.I4.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I4.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I4.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I4.i3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,s)</annotation></semantics></math> is a Gaussian (normal) distributed random variable with variance <math id="S2.I4.i3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I4.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I4.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I4.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I4.i3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is a random variable,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I4.i3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I4.i3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I4.i3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I4.i3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is the ratio of mutation.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S2.I4.i3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">A reasonable value of variance <math id="S2.I4.i3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> is the second moment <math id="S2.I4.i3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{v}}</annotation></semantics></math> of AdamW optimization algorithm. Maybe need some scaling factor, which is a hyperparameter to be determined through some experiments.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Experiments</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have done some experiments on the basis of three GPT-2<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> models: Small (124M parameters, 12 layers), Large (774M parameters, 36 layers), and XL (1558M parameters, 48 layers). As Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 2 Method ‣ EOE: Evolutionary Optimization of Experts for Training Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, Koifish would divide these <span id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">full models</span> into some <span id="S3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">EOE models</span>. As shown in Table <a href="#S3" title="3 Experiments ‣ EOE: Evolutionary Optimization of Experts for Training Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, each expert has 6 or 8 layers. For example, in the case of GPT-2 XL, EOE model has 6 experts, each has only 328.6M parameters. Koifish would train these experts one by one. At each step, only load and update 328.6M parameters. After some steps, all 1558M parameters are updated. After the training process, Koifish only saves the best model, which only contains 328.6M parameters. It’s only one-fifth of the full model file.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">[ht]
<span id="S3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_caption ltx_align_center">Parameters of full models and EOE models</span>


<span id="S3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<span class="ltx_thead">
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.p2.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></span>
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.p2.1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Full Parameters</span></span>
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.p2.1.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Experts Number</span></span>
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.p2.1.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Layers in each expert</span></span>
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.p2.1.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameters of each expert</span></span></span>
</span>
<span class="ltx_tbody">
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">GPT2-small</span>
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">124M</span>
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">2</span>
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">6</span>
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">81M</span></span>
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">GPT2-large</span>
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">774M</span>
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">6</span>
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">6</span>
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">183M</span></span>
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">GPT2-XL</span>
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r">1558M</span>
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r">6</span>
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r">8</span>
<span id="S3.p2.1.2.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r">328.6M</span></span>
</span>
</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">All experiments are conducted on a single NVIDIA 4090 GPU with 24G memory <span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
            
            
            
          All detailed logs are available at <a href="https://github.com/gruai/koifish/tree/main/cases/gpt2/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/gruai/koifish/tree/main/cases/gpt2/</a></span></span></span>. The training and test datasets come from the FineWeb Edu 100B dataset<a href="https://karpathy/fineweb-edu-100B-gpt2-token-shards" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">karpathy/fineweb-edu-100B-gpt2-token-shards</a>, which is tokenized with GPT-2 tokenizer using the code in llm.c<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>.It includes about 1000 files. Each file contains 100M tokens. Our training only used five billion tokens of FineWeb.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S3" title="3 Experiments ‣ EOE: Evolutionary Optimization of Experts for Training Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> lists the training summary.</p>
<ol id="S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GPU Memory</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">EOE models need much less resource than full models. For example, in the case of GPT-2 XL, train an EOE model needs  23G memory, which is only one-fifth of that to train a full model.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Loss</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The loss of EOE models is slightly worse than the baseline that is from llm.c <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>( A pure c/cu reproduction of GPT2). We can optimistically estimate that this result can be further improverd. The EOE method has just been proposed, and there are still many ways to enhance its performance.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughput</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The throughput obtained using EOE method is very high. In the case of GPT2-XL, the throughput &gt; 50 k/second, which is at least fifty times that of training a full model. Actually, its really hard to train a full model in single 4090. It needs  118G memory, which is much greater than the 24G memory of 4090. So have to use some tricks(quantization, re-materialization, reduce batch-size to 1…). No matter what method, the throughput is less than 1 k/second. So in this experiment, the EOE framework accelerates the throughput more than fifty times!</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">[h]
<span id="S3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_caption ltx_align_center">Training summary of three experiments</span>


<span id="S3.p5.1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<span class="ltx_thead">
<span id="S3.p5.1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S3.p5.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.p5.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></span>
<span id="S3.p5.1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.p5.1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameters</span></span>
<span id="S3.p5.1.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.p5.1.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Loss (Baseline)</span></span>
<span id="S3.p5.1.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.p5.1.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">EOE Memory<sup id="S3.p5.1.2.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S3.p5.1.2.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">1</span></sup></span></span>
<span id="S3.p5.1.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.p5.1.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Full Memory<sup id="S3.p5.1.2.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S3.p5.1.2.1.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">2</span></sup></span></span>
<span id="S3.p5.1.2.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.p5.1.2.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Total time</span> <sup id="S3.p5.1.2.1.6.2" class="ltx_sup">3</sup></span>
<span id="S3.p5.1.2.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.p5.1.2.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Throughput</span></span></span>
</span>
<span class="ltx_tbody">
<span id="S3.p5.1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S3.p5.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">GPT2-small</span>
<span id="S3.p5.1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">124M</span>
<span id="S3.p5.1.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">3.287 (3.425)</span>
<span id="S3.p5.1.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>6.8G</span>
<span id="S3.p5.1.2.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>11.9G</span>
<span id="S3.p5.1.2.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>8 hours</span>
<span id="S3.p5.1.2.2.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>140k/s</span></span>
<span id="S3.p5.1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
